From e4c6e605cb5b7adc695379ae972292c0b705d969 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Stellman <andrew@stellman.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:59:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix readuntil() missing a separator split across chunks

StreamReader.readuntil() searched each buffered chunk separately, so a
multi-byte separator whose bytes arrived in different chunks was never
matched and the call returned data past it. Also check the last
len(separator) - 1 bytes already read together with the start of the
next chunk.
---
 CHANGES/PRNUMBER.bugfix.rst |   3 +
 CONTRIBUTORS.txt            |   1 +
 aiohttp/streams.py          |  19 ++++--
 tests/test_streams.py       | 124 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 142 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 CHANGES/PRNUMBER.bugfix.rst

diff --git a/CHANGES/PRNUMBER.bugfix.rst b/CHANGES/PRNUMBER.bugfix.rst
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..c1d6e2cf1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/CHANGES/PRNUMBER.bugfix.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+Fixed :py:meth:`~aiohttp.StreamReader.readuntil` not finding a multi-byte
+separator whose bytes arrived in different chunks, which made it return data
+past the separator -- by :user:`andrewstellman`.
